Elven dagger does 3:2 average damage small:large.  Dwarvish short sword
does 4:4.5 average damage.  BUT.  Any dagger gets +2 to hit.  It misses
far less often.  More hits, more damage.

> Just bad luck?

Good luck can get any weapon to hit nearly every time.  Since you just
started mines end, you very likely had a luck level of 0.

> Possibly having found an uncursed sword with negative enchantment?

Maybe.  The dagger's to-hit bonus was probably it.

There are no short sword artifacts, so there is little use advancing
skill in short sword for any character class unless you are trying for
an artifactless ascension.

If you get in trouble on a mine level, beeline for the stairs and head
up.  You were too aggressive right then.

